# Files every branch adds to, at the same places: merged with git's union
# driver, which keeps both sides' lines where both added some (no conflict
# markers). On 2026-11-13 every merge train stopped on CHANGELOG.md's
# "### Fixed" list and TEST_MAP.md's newest rows. Safe here because these are
# lists of independent lines; the cost is that two edits of the SAME line
# both survive -- read `git diff HEAD^1 -- <file>` after a train merge.
# TEST_MAP row ids: a branch writes `| Mnew |`; `tools/test-map-ids.py
# assign` numbers them on the train, and `check` (in the gate) fails a
# duplicate.
CHANGELOG.md            merge=union
docs/dev/TEST_MAP.md    merge=union
